# Paragraph emphasis

When body copy uses *asterisk-wrapped* emphasis (or a dedicated emphasized paragraph line), emphasized text gets **bold weight** and **`--section-emphasis` color**. It must inherit the paragraph's font size and letter-spacing — never override tracking or text size on the `<em>`.

## Tokens

Use the shared classes from `@/lib/typography`:

- **`paragraphEmphasisClassName`** — body paragraphs (`font-bold` + emphasis color)
- **`headingEmphasisClassName`** — headings only (color only; weight comes from the heading)

Parse inline emphasis with `parseEmphasis(text, emphasis, "paragraph")`.

## Examples

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — inline paragraph emphasis
<p className={bodyXlClassName}>
  {parseEmphasis("*Rescued food* reaches neighbors.", true, "paragraph")}
</p>

// ✅ GOOD — full emphasized paragraph line (HeroContentCard bodyEmphasis)
<p className={cn(bodyClasses[bodySize], "font-bold text-[var(--section-emphasis)]")}>
  {parseEmphasis(bodyEmphasis, emphasis, "paragraph")}
</p>

// ❌ BAD — semibold or custom tracking on emphasized paragraph text
<em className="font-semibold tracking-[-0.01em] text-[var(--section-emphasis)]">...</em>

// ❌ BAD — heading emphasis token on body copy
{parseEmphasis(body, true, "heading")}
```

## Headings

Headings keep `headingEmphasisClassName` (color only). Do not add `font-bold` to emphasized runs inside section headings — those inherit the heading's `font-medium`.
